# LifePunch — Model Usage Law (July 2026)

**Canonical:** `lifepunch/docs/OPUS_USAGE_LAW.md`

## Core law

> Use the weakest model that fits. Escalate to Opus the moment genuine complexity appears.
> Plan once → implement one slice → flatgrass proof → review once. Do not burn frontier models re-deriving context.

**Primary IDE: GitHub Copilot on VENGEANCE.**
**Grok lane: Cursor** — only for `GROK REQUIRED` tasks (Grok Build 1 not available in Copilot).

## Model tiers (Copilot)

| Tier | Model | When |
|------|-------|------|
| **Tier 1** | Claude Opus 4.8 (manually select) | Architecture · multi-file C# · economy/auth · security/legal/structural synthesis · cross-system debugging |
| **Tier 2B** | Claude Sonnet 4.6 (Copilot default) | Scoped edits · docs · search · validators · commit messages · straightforward Q&A (~80% of work) |
| **Tier 2A** | Grok Build 1 (Cursor only) | `GROK REQUIRED` → open Cursor · bounded Razor/SCSS · repo-grounded technical planning · ModelDoc maps |
| **Tier 3** | Cornerman local LM | `GREEN CODE/DEEP REQUIRED` → via `cornerman-lm` MCP · distill · prep · bulk summarize |

## Task route tags

Honor any route tag on a task. If the required route is not active, **switch to it or stop and tell Bloodwave** — never silently substitute.

| Tag | Do |
|-----|----|
| `AUTO OK` | Claude Sonnet 4.6 (Copilot default) |
| `OPUS REQUIRED` | Manually select Claude Opus 4.8 in Copilot |
| `GROK REQUIRED` | Open Cursor → select Grok Build 1 |
| `GREEN CODE REQUIRED` | Cornerman / LM Studio Qwen Coder (Tier-3 candidate) |
| `GREEN DEEP REQUIRED` | Cornerman / LM Studio Qwen dense (Tier-3 distill/warm) |

**Never let default Sonnet silently substitute** for: economy · persistence · `[Sync(FromHost)]` · RPCs · purchase
routing · migration · power/link state machines · terminal defense · final major-slice / commit-critical review.

## Use Opus for

Architecture · debugging · MCP workflows · ModelDoc setup · multi-file C# · Razor UI **blockers** · agent planning (Phase 1, no code).

## Use Sonnet (default) for

README · changelogs · Discord · marketing · doc formatting · scoped refactors · boilerplate.

## Four-phase workflow (major tasks)

| Phase | Model | What |
|-------|-------|------|
| **1** | Opus | Plan only — files, risks, definition of done. **No code.** |
| **2** | Opus | Implement **one slice only** |
| **3** | Any + bridge | **Flatgrass** play proof — not editor-only |
| **4** | Opus | Review — find defects before next slice |

One focused chat per major task; fresh chat + short summary for the next phase.

## lifepunchbitcoin ship order (strict scope)

Exclusively on **one entity until flatgrass proof + owner sign-off**, then advance:

1. **Hub** (`lpbitcoin/bitcoinhub`) — active
2. **Terminal** — after Hub Phase A + H10
3. **GPU Rack** — after Terminal baseline

Hub Opus slices (one per Phase 2): collision validation → power state → fan anim → LED state machine → telemetry overlays → interaction polish.

